From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] device-libs: refresh checks for upstream LLVM 24 lowering

Preserve IR names and check the renamed synchronization metadata. Bound
register checks at the kernel end instead of scanning generated kernel
implementation functions. Check equivalent finite-value comparisons,
promoted native rsqrt and NaN-preserving min lowering rather than obsolete
address calculations and instruction sequences.

Add exact special-value lgamma_r constant checks. The complete upstream
fixture remains intact: system LLVM does not fold all target reciprocal
intrinsics used by its large-argument cases.

--- a/amd/device-libs/test/compile/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/amd/device-libs/test/compile/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@

 foreach(gpu gfx900 gfx1030)
   add_constant_fold_test(lgamma_r ${gpu})
+  add_constant_fold_test(lgamma_special ${gpu})
 endforeach()

 foreach(gpu gfx803)
